WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.618
Hello, I’m Robert Schaub.

2
00:00:02.760 --> 00:00:07.275
I spent 38 years in software engineering and project leadership—

3
00:00:07.416 --> 00:00:10.335
30 years at Phonak/Sonova.

4
00:00:10.477 --> 00:00:19.863
I founded FactHarbor Verein, a Swiss non-profit, and built FactHarbor’s working Alpha and Our AI Charter Runtime, a proof of concept.

5
00:00:20.005 --> 00:00:24.909
My motivation is societal: facts are a foundation of democracy.

6
00:00:25.051 --> 00:00:30.341
I want AI to strengthen, not weaken, responsibility for decisions.

7
00:00:30.483 --> 00:00:35.573
Evidence is essential, but a consequential answer also needs valid authority,

8
00:00:35.714 --> 00:00:40.863
a decision before effect, and a record affected people can inspect and challenge.

9
00:00:41.004 --> 00:00:48.466
FactHarbor has already analysed a public claim that a heat pump can be recommended for an existing residential building in Winterthur

10
00:00:48.607 --> 00:00:51.000
without first checking the building.

11
00:00:51.141 --> 00:00:58.258
The Alpha judged that claim false and showed supporting and opposing evidence, sources, limitations and uncertainty.

12
00:00:58.399 --> 00:01:01.637
Evidence-Gated Agents will test the next step.

13
00:01:01.778 --> 00:01:06.188
For the prototype, FactHarbor will prepare assessed claims.

14
00:01:06.329 --> 00:01:09.539
An AI may draft an exact answer from them,

15
00:01:09.681 --> 00:01:15.599
but a gateway outside the model decides whether current authority and declared evidence support its release.

16
00:01:15.741 --> 00:01:19.894
If it stops, a different answer cannot inherit approval:

17
00:01:20.036 --> 00:01:23.198
it must be prepared and checked as a new proposal.

18
00:01:23.339 --> 00:01:31.009
If released, the recipient receives an inspectable receipt linking the answer, authority, evidence, decision and outcome.

19
00:01:31.150 --> 00:01:37.483
Beyond the prototype, I want to develop evidence-gated decision-making applications and services

20
00:01:37.625 --> 00:01:42.185
for companies, public bodies, newsrooms and civil society.

21
00:01:42.327 --> 00:01:49.257
With permission, they could weigh an organisation’s policies, contracts and records alongside public evidence.

22
00:01:49.399 --> 00:01:54.184
People affected by an answer should be able to understand it, challenge it,

23
00:01:54.325 --> 00:01:57.253
and seek correction or independent review.

24
00:01:57.395 --> 00:02:01.145
I built both foundations and can integrate them directly.

25
00:02:01.287 --> 00:02:07.912
The Prototype Fund’s coaches and cohort can challenge my assumptions, improve the recipient experience,

26
00:02:08.054 --> 00:02:12.729
and help me reach practitioners who can test whether the receipt is understandable

27
00:02:12.870 --> 00:02:16.832
and where AI adds justified value over simpler methods.

28
00:02:16.974 --> 00:02:22.092
My vision is a free and fair society in which technology strengthens democracy

29
00:02:22.233 --> 00:02:28.208
because consequential decisions remain authorised, evidence-grounded and open to challenge.

